            <ArticleTitle>Complications of vasectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The most common complications of vasectomy are ecchymosis and sperm granuloma. A sperm granuloma may increase the chance of spontaneous recanalization. Orchitis and epididymitis generally respond best to treatment with anti-inflammatory drugs and antibiotics. Although antibodies frequently develop against different portions of the sperm, long-term studies have not shown any adverse effects of these antibodies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
